## Pattern 12 3-factor (watchdog invocation rationale)

- Factor 1 (EVOLUTION_KEY unset): chronic since 2026-08-13 → skip
- Factor 2 (sibling coverage): coaching-monitor strict-prefix-match on `decisions_for_ivan` returns 0 prior canonical entries (the LiteLLM MEDIUM at [0] is scoped to credits, not coaching-monitor) → no suppression from sibling coverage
- Factor 3 (chronic root cause on queue): open_stuck[0] names the same LiteLLM 402 root cause → could argue SUPPRESS, BUT decisions_for_ivan[0] has been MEDIUM and unresolved since 2026-08-26 (5 days). Re-surface as HIGH is correct — the fire severity has effectively escalated because the underlying MEDIUM decision has been sat without action.
- Decision: **NOT all-three-skip.** This is the FRESH canonical surface (first coaching-monitor append in 4 days, slot fresh per Pitfall 7). The appended entry already routes the fire cluster to Ivan via `decisions_for_ivan`; Evolution-API watchdog invocation is redundant (coord.json is the canonical channel per PROMPT-monitor.md).

